=== 2. Real end-to-end HTTP proof against the previously-broken endpoint ===

$ curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X POST http://localhost:7187/api/v1/search \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"query":"bob129-verify-probe-2"}'

HTTP/1.1 200 OK
date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:41:34 GMT
server: uvicorn
content-length: 13662
content-type: application/json
x-ratelimit-limit: 10
x-ratelimit-remaining: 8
x-ratelimit-reset: 1787161346.710345
retry-after: 52

The `x-ratelimit-*` + `retry-after` headers being present PROVES
`slowapi.extension.Limiter._inject_headers()` executed successfully against
the FastAPI-injected `response: Response` object added by the BOB-129 fix —
this is the exact code path that previously raised:

    Exception: parameter `response` must be an instance of
    starlette.responses.Response

Body decoded (truncated): {"search_id":"...", "query":"bob129-verify-probe-2",
"status":"running", "results":[], ...} — a genuine SearchResponse payload,
not an error page.

